  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat annual interest rate does Jane's savings account offer? Jane has saved $5 from her allowance every week for the past 8 weeks. Jane will continue saving the same amount every two weeks. Jane keeps her allowance savings in an account that pays 2% annual interest. The account compounds interest once at the end of each year.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "EXACT PUBLIC STATE AFTER TURN 1; NO PRIVATE OR FUTURE DATA\nPUBLIC_STATE_JSON:\n{\"completed_task_turns\":[{\"turn\":1,\"user_message\":\"Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\\\boxed{}.\\n\\nWhat annual interest rate does Jane's savings account offer? Jane has saved $5 from her allowance every week for the past 8 weeks. Jane will continue saving the same amount every two weeks. Jane keeps her allowance savings in an account that pays 2% annual interest. The account compounds interest once at the end of each year.\"}],\"public_metadata\":{\"benchmark\":\"Evolving Intent GSM8K\",\"upstream_commit\":\"993d6be9597ac03854b46362ccd647eb1bfd267a\"}}",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Jane has saved $4 from her allowance every week for the past 8 weeks.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The account’s annual interest rate is explicitly given as **2%**. Changing Jane’s weekly savings from $5 to $4 does not change the interest rate; it only changes the amount in the account.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Jane will continue saving the same amount each week.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Jane will continue saving **$4 each week**, but this does not affect the account’s stated interest rate. The account pays **2% annual interest**, compounded once at the end of each year.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: Jane's allowance savings are measured in dollars per week.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Jane saves **$4 per week**, and the account pays an annual interest rate of **2%**, compounded once per year. The savings frequency and dollar-per-week units affect the balance, not the stated interest rate.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\% \\text{ per year}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How much money will Jane have saved from her allowance after one full year? Also, here's some more context: Jane saves money for 52 weeks in a year. This calculation ignores any interest earned in the account.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Jane saves **$4 per week** for **52 weeks**:\n\n\\[\n4 \\times 52 = 208\n\\]\n\nIgnoring interest, Jane will have saved:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$208}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Her weekly saving rate is constant throughout the year.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since Jane saves a constant **$4 per week** for **52 weeks**:\n\n\\[\n4 \\times 52 = 208\n\\]\n\nIgnoring interest, Jane will have saved:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$208}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many more weeks will Jane need to save to have a total savings of $60? By the way, Jane wants to have saved a total of $60.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Jane has already saved:\n\n\\[\n8 \\times \\$4=\\$32\n\\]\n\nShe needs:\n\n\\[\n\\$60-\\$32=\\$28\n\\]\n\nAt a rate of \\(\\$4\\) per week, the additional time required is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\$28}{\\$4\\text{/week}}=7\\text{ weeks}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{7\\text{ weeks}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
